📐 BMI Formula

BMI is calculated using:
BMI = weight / (height × height)


Where:

Weight is measured in kilograms (kg)
Height is measured in meters (m)
Example
Weight = 70 kg
Height = 1.75 m

Calculation:

BMI = 70 / (1.75 × 1.75)
BMI = 22.86
📊 BMI Categories

The program uses the following categories:

BMI Range	Category
BMI < 18.5	Underweight
18.5 ≤ BMI < 25	Normal weight
25 ≤ BMI < 30	Overweight
BMI ≥ 30	Obese
⚙️ How It Works

The program follows these steps:

Displays the BMI Calculator heading.
Asks the user to enter their weight.
The user can enter q to quit.
Asks the user to enter their height.
Converts the input values to floating-point numbers.
Calculates the BMI using the BMI formula.
Rounds the BMI to 2 decimal places.
Checks the BMI against the different categories.
Displays the BMI and category.
Repeats the process until the user enters q.


