⚠️ Handling Height of 0

A height of 0 would cause a division-by-zero error because the BMI formula divides by height squared.

The program handles this using:


try:
    bmi = kg / (height * height)


except ZeroDivisionError:
    print("Invaid height of 0 Enter correct height")


Instead of crashing, the program displays a friendly error message.


